            <ArticleTitle>[Anesthetic management of concomitant off-pump coronary artery bypass grafting and complete pneumonectomy for lung cancer].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1273-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 69-year-old man was scheduled for combined surgery involving off-pump coronary artery bypass grafting (OPCABG) for coronary stenosis and total pneumonectomy for lung cancer. Anesthesia was maintained with fentanyl, thiopental, sevoflurane, nitrous oxide, and epidural anesthesia using 1.0% mepivacaine. Although a steady hemodynamic circulation was maintained during OPCABG, it was difficult to stabilize the circulation during the total pneumonectomy.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
